The JSONL fixtures preserve actual CLI event shapes from isolated synthetic requests through the Copilot proxy.
The clients were Claude Code 2.1.294 and Codex CLI 0.161.0.
Session identifiers, tool identifiers, signatures, child identifiers, and temporary home paths use fixture placeholders.
Debug progress events are omitted because the completion parser does not consume them.
Duplicate JSON keys are preserved where the CLI emitted them.
Original outputs remain private diagnostics and are not included here.

claude_bare_search_unavailable.jsonl records minimal mode without a search tool.
claude_search_upstream_error.jsonl records two WebSearch tool failures with upstream HTTP 400.
claude_agent_completed.jsonl records a completed Agent result containing the child answer 323.
codex_delegation_uninvoked.jsonl records an assistant claiming delegation without a tool call.
codex_search_different_ids.jsonl records search start and completion events with different identifiers.
codex_wait_without_spawn.jsonl records a wait call without a spawned child or completed child state.
codex_ephemeral_spawn_failure.json preserves the actual follow-up function_call_output for a failed full-history child spawn.
The isolated Codex invocation used --ephemeral, so its parent model context had no persisted rollout.
codex_v2_parent_completed.jsonl and codex_v2_child_completed.jsonl preserve the actual successful parent and child rollout chain.
Unrelated model instructions and context rows are omitted or replaced with fixture text.
The child session links to the current parent and contains its own completed turn and answer 323.
The parent contains the actual spawn result, wait result, and child handback.

Codex CLI 0.161.0 records V2 spawn calls in its persisted rollout but emits no spawn ThreadItem in JSONL stdout.
Its V2 wait ThreadItem leaves receiver_thread_ids and agents_states empty because it waits for mailbox activity.
The acceptance check supplements stdout with the verified native rollout chain and preserves the original V1 event gate.
Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/core/src/tools/handlers/multi_agents_v2/spawn.rs
Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/core/src/tools/handlers/multi_agents_v2/wait.rs
